  "primary_conclusion": "Study 008 prospectively captured a contemporaneous public authority boundary and found all 63 governed leaf values with unique selectors and provenance. However, one required cross-source canonical binding failed: the governing MRD names the Naturepedia reference implementation as Naturepedia while the canonical Naturepedia page names it Naturepedia™. Because the frozen policy treats the trademark mark as meaningful and forbids normalization, the authority boundary was not internally exact enough to authorize target construction or model measurement.",
  "methodological_conclusion": "Exact leaf availability is necessary but not sufficient for a governed-state benchmark. A prospective authority package must also bind the same entities consistently across its governing surfaces. Study 008 therefore isolates an authority-coherence failure before target construction, preventing the failure from being misattributed to model behavior.",
